From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence runtime tails and share capture storage
 budget [daveey]

Draft gap4 continuation, not production-enabled. Bind runtime tail receipts to sealed event bytes and deadline, track in-flight actual urgency reads, snapshot bounded detached payload primitives, and charge root/runtime metadata plus temporary file peaks under a cross-process advisory lock. Runtime arming/startup and assembled export remain incomplete. RED late-seal and caller-mutation tests reproduced; 366 consumer tests passed then 29 runtime/budget cases passed including spawned process contention. No live capture or policy changes.
